---
description: KIS Creativity Space — item areas (categories) manager on the admin Items tab
alwaysApply: true
---

- This folder is a design handoff; README.md is the source of truth (chips UI, add/remove rules, consumers).
- Areas are ONE managed ordered list; every area dropdown and the public Resources grouping read it — no hardcoded area arrays left anywhere.
- Effective list = stored areas ∪ areas still referenced by items; an item must never point at a missing area.
- Remove is only offered for empty areas (confirm dialog) and never for the last remaining area; enforce server-side too (409 when items exist).
- Duplicates rejected case-insensitively on trimmed names, with the inline "already exists" error in the UI.
- Adding an area pre-selects it in the add-item form; removing one resets selects that pointed at it (QR filter → "All areas").
- No rename in this pass — do not add it speculatively.
- designs/KIS Admin.dc.html is a browser-openable prototype for reference only — never import or port support.js.
